# Firmware Rules

## Defines (top of main.cpp — filled before flashing)
#define SSID          "UCSD-PROTECTED"
#define WIFI_PASS     "..."
#define SERVER_URL    "https://api.ethanha.com/api/reading"
#define API_KEY       "[DEVICE_API_KEY value from .env]"
#define COURT_ID      1        // change per device for each court
#define PIR_PIN       13
#define FALLBACK_S    300      // 5 min fallback if server unreachable
#define MAX_SLEEP_S   3600     // 1hr cap — ESP32 timer limit

## Deep Sleep Pattern
- RTC_DATA_ATTR int bootCount survives deep sleep
- On bootCount == 1: delay(60000) for PIR sensor warmup
- After every action: call esp_deep_sleep_start() — loop() is always empty
- Sleep duration comes from server response sleep_seconds field
- Always cap sleep at MAX_SLEEP_S before passing to timer

## WiFi Pattern
- Try 20 times with 500ms delay between attempts
- On failure: sleep FALLBACK_S and retry — never hang indefinitely

## HTTP Pattern
- Use WiFiClientSecure + HTTPClient
- client.setInsecure() is acceptable for prototype
- POST body: {"court_id": COURT_ID, "occupied": true/false}
- Header: X-API-Key: API_KEY
- Parse response JSON with ArduinoJson StaticJsonDocument<128>
- On any HTTP error: return FALLBACK_S from sendReading()

## Never
- Never use delay() in the main loop (use deep sleep instead)
- Never use String concatenation in a loop (heap fragmentation)
- Never expose API_KEY in comments or serial output
